# Draft delivery lineage exported by the Proposal Workbench (BRSF software-development profile). Refine, then validate with the BRSF validator.

ex:Mission a backlog:Mission ; rdfs:label "CertiChain: Verifiable Blockchain Certificates for University Club Events"@en ; backlog:hasMissionStatement "CertiChain lets an IKU student club issue event certificates whose authenticity anyone can check in seconds. The event organiser issues certificates from a simple dashboard; each certificate's fingerprint is recorded on a public blockchain. Every certificate holder gets a PDF with a QR code, and any verifier can confirm it is genuine and not revoked without contacting the club or trusting a central server." ; backlog:hasMissionOutcome "Once CertiChain exists, a certificate holder can send a single link that proves their certificate is genuine, a verifier can check it in under ten seconds without e-mailing anyone, and the club can revoke a wrong certificate publicly, even after the board that issued it has graduated." ; backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_SessionDrafted .
ex:Lineage a backlog:Lineage ; backlog:lineageForMission ex:Mission ; backlog:adoptsObligationSet backlog:OS_SDLC_v2 .
ex:Customer1 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "IKU Computer Club (Istanbul Kültür University student club)"@en ; rdfs:comment "Customer (owner): A free, tamper-proof way to issue participation certificates for its workshops and events that anyone can check in seconds, without the club searching Excel and Google Drive files to answer verification requests."@en .
ex:EndUser1 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "Event organiser"@en ; rdfs:comment "End user: Club board member who runs a workshop or event - Uploads the attendance list after an event, issues the certificates and revokes one issued by mistake (monthly, Laptop browser with the MetaMask wallet)"@en .
ex:EndUser2 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "Certificate holder"@en ; rdfs:comment "End user: IKU student who attended a club event - Downloads the PDF certificate, adds it to a CV or LinkedIn profile and shares the verification link (occasional, Phone or laptop browser)"@en .
ex:EndUser3 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "Verifier"@en ; rdfs:comment "End user: Employer, internship coordinator or another university's staff member - Scans the QR code or uploads the PDF to check that the certificate is genuine and not revoked (occasional, Phone camera or laptop browser, no wallet needed)"@en .
