ex:G2 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "The registry contract issues, revokes and verifies certificates and is deployed on Sepolia"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A1 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "Without the contract there is no tamper-proof record to check against." .
ex:G3 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "The organiser can issue a whole event's certificates from the dashboard in one batch"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A2 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "If issuing is harder than the current template, the club will not use the system." .
ex:G4 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Every certificate follows one JSON-LD format and passes the SHACL shape before issue"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A4 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "A single checked format keeps hashes reproducible and certificates readable by others." .
ex:G5 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "No work goes into features outside the four areas, and no personal data is written on chain"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Containment ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A1 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "Keeps a one-term team effort focused and keeps the project KVKK-safe." .
ex:Spec a backlog:Specification ; backlog:hasSpecificationText "The system has three parts. A CertificateRegistry smart contract on Sepolia keeps a mapping from a certificate hash to its issuer, issue time and revocation status; only wallets holding the ISSUER role may call issue or revoke, and anyone may call verify for free. The issuer dashboard lets an event organiser connect MetaMask, enter event details and upload a CSV of participants; the certificate service builds one JSON-LD certificate per participant, validates it against the SHACL shape, salts and hashes it with SHA-256, and the dashboard submits all hashes in one batch transaction. The service then produces a PDF per participant with a QR code linking to the verification page. The verification page, needing no wallet, reads the certificate ID from the link or recomputes the hash from an uploaded file, queries the contract through a public RPC endpoint and shows Valid, Revoked or Not found, with the issuing club and date. Names and student numbers stay off chain." .
ex:Scen1 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Nominal ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a certificate issued by the club for the Git workshop, when a verifier scans its QR code, then the page shows Valid with the club name and issue date." .
ex:Scen2 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Rejection ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a certificate PDF whose participant name was edited after issue, when a verifier uploads it, then the recomputed hash is not found and the page shows Not found." .
ex:Scen3 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Rejection ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a wallet without the ISSUER role, when it calls issue on the contract, then the transaction reverts and no certificate is recorded." .
ex:Scen4 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Boundary ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a certificate that the organiser has revoked, when a verifier checks it, then the page shows Revoked with the revocation date instead of Valid." .
ex:Scen5 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Absent ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given an empty CSV attendance file, when the organiser starts issuing, then the dashboard stops with an error and sends no transaction." .
