ex:O2 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Share of contract functions covered by passing Hardhat tests"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G2 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Derived ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "solidity-coverage report on the CertificateRegistry contract in CI" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0%" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "At least 90% line coverage, all tests passing" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O3 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Time for the organiser to issue certificates for a 30-person event"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G3 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Stopwatch during a trial with the club's organiser, from CSV upload to all PDFs ready" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "Made by hand from a template; time to be measured at the club's first December workshop" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "Under 5 minutes" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Decrease .
ex:O4 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Share of issued certificates that pass the SHACL shape"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G4 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Derived ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Validation run over all issued JSON-LD files in CI, conforming / total" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "No format exists (0%)" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "100%" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Hold .
ex:O5 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Personal data fields written on chain"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G5 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Review of contract storage and event logs for names, e-mails or student numbers" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Hold .
ex:Model_Activity a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_ActivityDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "1. The organiser runs the event and exports the attendance list as CSV. 2. The organiser connects MetaMask to the dashboard; if the wallet has no ISSUER role, the flow stops with an error. 3. The organiser enters event details and uploads the CSV; if the file is empty or malformed, the dashboard rejects it. 4. The service builds and SHACL-validates one certificate per row; invalid rows are listed for correction. 5. The dashboard sends one batch transaction; on failure nothing is recorded and the organiser may retry. 6. The organiser downloads the PDFs with QR codes as one ZIP file and shares them with the attendees . 7. A verifier opens the QR link; the page queries the contract and branches to Valid, Revoked or Not found." .
ex:Model_Sequence a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_SequenceDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "Organiser → Dashboard: upload CSV and event details. Dashboard → Certificate service: POST /api/issue. Certificate service: builds one certificate per row, validates it, hashes it and renders its PDF with a QR code. Service → Dashboard: hashes and PDFs. Dashboard → MetaMask: request signature for issueBatch(hashes). MetaMask → Registry contract: transaction. Contract → Dashboard: CertificateIssued events; dashboard shows the Etherscan link and the ZIP download. Verifier → Verification page: open QR link with the hash, or upload the PDF. Page → Public RPC → Registry contract: verify(hash). Contract → Page: status, issuer, issue and revoke time. Page → Verifier: Valid, Revoked or Not found." .
ex:Model_Class a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_ClassDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "CertificateRegistry (contract): uses OpenZeppelin AccessControl with ISSUER_ROLE; records: mapping(bytes32 => Record); functions issue(bytes32), issueBatch(bytes32[]) (at most 200 hashes), revoke(bytes32), verify(bytes32) returns (status, issuer, issuedAt, revokedAt) where status is NotFound, Valid or Revoked; errors EmptyHash, AlreadyIssued, NotIssued, AlreadyRevoked, BadBatchSize. Record (struct): issuer: address; issuedAt: uint64; revokedAt: uint64 (0 while the certificate is valid). Certificate (off chain, W3C VC JSON-LD): id: URI; issuer: Issuer; validFrom: dateTime; credentialSubject: recipientName, recipientEmail, eventTitle, eventDate, hours; wasGeneratedBy: Event; salt: string. Its SHA-256 hash of the canonical JSON is the bytes32 key; the hash is not a field of the certificate. Event: title, date. Issuer: club name, wallet address (did:pkh). Relations: an Event has many Certificates; a Certificate belongs to one Participant and one Issuer; a Record stores the hash of exactly one Certificate." .
